# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# React Router owns every path after the first load, so the server has
# to answer /projects/<id> and /reset-password with index.html rather
# than a 404 - otherwise a refresh or a pasted link dead-ends. This is
# the Pages equivalent of the rewrite in vercel.json.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the URL in the address bar has to stay put, so
# the router still sees the path it was asked for.
#
# Anything Vite emitted (/assets/*, /favicon.svg, ...) is a real file
# and is served before this rule is consulted, so the wildcard is safe.
/*    /index.html   200
